Z||000000||speed racer||08-13-2001||10:31 PM||||Has any one ever ported and polished their V-6 intake if so how much trouble was it to take the intake upper and lower in and out of the car. How much did it cost to get it ported was. Was there any performance increases||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||08-13-2001||10:41 PM||||Mine's all apart right now, and the lower is fairly accessible, the middle is not completely accessible, and the upper section is virtually impossible. <BR>I think gasket matching the ports and extrude honing would be the best way to go.<BR>There are also a lot of mold parting lines that I think would be beneficial to clean up.  The heads aren't too bad to get to, since the intake runner is so short in the ctlinder head itself.<BR>I smoothed my lower section fairly well with my dremel and some sandpaper, but mostly just to clean the crap out more than anything.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||08-13-2001||10:44 PM||||I had my lower intake ported by Darrel Morse.<BR>I also had the t-body and upper plenum bored out by him. Hard to say if the lower intake helped or not since it was put on with my new engine but the lower intake is supposed to be one of the most restrictive parts of the intake system.<BR>You can reach Darrel via email at:<BR>morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||08-14-2001||12:29 AM||||If you can't get to it by hand, send it ti extrude hone.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
